00:00:03.339 --> 00:00:04.172
- The show is almost over

00:00:04.172 --> 00:00:06.610
but first let's do one last
story to give you a smile.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.347
Hopefully this is What I'm Liking.

00:00:08.347 --> 00:00:10.256
(ethereal music)

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:11.130
(audience claps)

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.750
Check out these pictures
y'all they look just

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.010
like old pinup posters, the red lipstick,

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.860
the innocent poses, the
waving American flags right?

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.470
Well, every one of the
women in those photos

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.460
is a military veteran modeling

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.210
to help raise money
for other vets in need.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.450
It's all part of the
nonprofit pinups for vets.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.360
And we have the founder

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.000
of the organization on the line right now.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.023
So everybody say hi to Gina Elise, hi.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.100
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.990
- Oh, you look beautiful.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.270
- I love that whole vibe.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.103
Oh, it's so beautiful.

00:00:41.103 --> 00:00:42.890
So tell us more about Pin-ups for Vets

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.550
and how it all got started.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.730
- Yeah, so it was basically back in 2006,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.730
there were a lot of stories in the news

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.980
about our troops coming back

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.800
from Iraq, needing medical care.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.250
And I felt so strongly

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.270
that I wanted to do something to help out.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.780
And I've always been a big fan
of World War II Pin Up Art.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.760
So I took my love of that art

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.564
to create a fundraising Pin Up Calendar

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:07.090
that we could use to support
our veterans and troops today.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.520
So we do everything from
a 50 state, military

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.230
and VA hospital tour, where
we actually take the calendars

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.830
into the hospitals to deliver
as gifts of appreciation

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:20.010
to buying rehab equipment
for veterans, hospitals.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:23.010
To doing these morale, boosting
makeovers for military wives

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.340
and female veterans, to
shipping care packages

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.900
to troops around the world.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.330
And we've been doing this for 16 years.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.273
- Oh, that's amazing.

00:01:30.273 --> 00:01:31.310
(audience claps)

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.920
Congratulations on all the success.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.460
And you also say this is a lot

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.950
about female empowerment as well, right?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:37.860
- Yes, yes.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.210
Basically back in 2014, we
started getting inquiries

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.890
from female veterans to volunteer with us.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.250
So I started taking them
into the VA hospitals with us

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.570
and the patients were
shocked that the ladies

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:53.130
standing next to me decked
out in 1940s, Pin Up outfits

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.470
were also veterans.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.890
And so I decided to start
putting these incredible ladies

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.410
in the calendar.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.380
A lot of times when we think of a veteran,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.830
we might think of a man.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.750
But there's such incredible women

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.660
that have stepped up to serve our country.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.060
And so I like to think that

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.370
this is really kind of
shifting the perception

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.410
about what a veteran is.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:13.930
In our 2022 calendar

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.730
we have a female black
Hawk helicopter pilot.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.330
We have an army doctor.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.100
And a lot of times the ladies tell me

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.480
that this has really helped
them to reclaim their femininity

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.980
after getting out of the military

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.480
and to embrace that
feminine side of themselves

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.305
that they had to put on the back burner.

00:02:29.305 --> 00:02:30.138
(audience claps)

00:02:30.138 --> 00:02:32.626
- Absolutely, thank you so much Gina,

00:02:32.626 --> 00:02:34.571
At least I'm liking your
post right now, right?

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:35.404
(beeps)

00:02:35.404 --> 00:02:36.683
- Thank you.

00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:38.710
- And that's not all, y'all
our season long partner,

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:40.410
Pilot Pen makers of G2.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.400
The go to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.330
They want to honor ultimate over achievers

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.163
just like you ma'am.

00:02:45.163 --> 00:02:46.070
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.545
for $1000, how does that sound?

00:02:47.545 --> 00:02:48.998
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.998 --> 00:02:50.898
- Thank you so much, Kelly, thank you.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.240
- Absolutely, absolutely thank you so much

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.193
for joining us today.

